load @term/seed/structure/space/vector
  find vector-space

# A tensor: a multilinear object on a vector space, a machine that eats vectors and covectors and returns a scalar,
# linearly in each slot. Scalars, vectors, and linear maps are low-rank tensors, and the metric and the curvature of a
# manifold are tensors. They are the language in which the laws of physics are written coordinate-free. The form carries
# the underlying vector space; the rank and the multilinearity are the tensor's shape.
form tensor
  link space, like vector-space
